    {
      "id": "7ec3405b-ab22-4264-b930-d8d736c98cbf",
      "type": "event",
      "date": "2026-05-22T00:00:00.000Z",
      "title": "TVS Venu Management And Consultancy Services Private Limited completed the acquisition of 4.90% stake in Jana Small Finance Bank Limited (NSEI:JSFB) from Jana Holdings Limited.",
      "body": "TVS Venu Management And Consultancy Services Private Limited agreed to acquire 4.90% stake in Jana Small Finance Bank Limited (NSEI:JSFB) from Jana Holdings Limited for INR 1.9 billion on May 18, 2026.\r\n\r\nThe expected completion of the transaction is May 18, 2026 to August 18, 2026. Ayush Katyayana, Nisha Nahata, Aditya Prasad and Kritika Dobhal of Cyril Amarchand Mangaldas acted as legal advisor to Jana Holdings Limited. Haigreve Khaitan of Khaitan & Co.acted as legal advisor to TVS Venu Management And Consultancy Services Private Limited.\r\n\n\nTVS Venu Management And Consultancy Services Private Limited completed the acquisition of 4.90% stake in Jana Small Finance Bank Limited (NSEI:JSFB) from Jana Holdings Limited on May 22, 2026.",
      "keyDevTypeId": "81",
      "source_url": null,
      "raw_subtype": "EventActivity"
    },
    {
      "id": "64e36fb9-c228-40e8-9f85-253b57d28c45",
      "type": "event",
      "date": "2026-05-16T00:00:00.000Z",
      "title": "TVS, Other Investors Reportedly Keen to Buy into Jana Small Finance Bank",
      "body": "A clutch of new investors, including Venu Srinivasan-led TVS Venu Group, would buy into Jana Small Finance Bank Limited (NSEI:JSFB), while the lender's long-time partner TPG Capital (TPG Capital, L.P.) is likely to partially reduce its stake, people aware said. The total fundraise for the universal bank aspirant is likely to be up to INR 7,000 million. The infusion would involve a combination of primary and secondary deals, said the people cited above. The TVS Venu Group is looking to acquire a 10% stake in the bank for about INR 4,500 million. According to industry sources, three to four other investors are lined up for making investments in the bank, which is the fourth largest small finance bank in terms of gross loan portfolio. An overseas corporation has shown interest too. Jana is li",
      "keyDevTypeId": "65",
      "source_url": null,
      "raw_subtype": "EventActivity"
    },
    {
      "id": "76d8a9f9-39d1-4c6e-aa38-76050f121174",
      "type": "brief",
      "date": "2026-05-05T11:46:30.000Z",
      "title": "Full year 2026 earnings: EPS and revenues exceed analyst expectations",
      "body": "Full year 2026 results: EPS: ₹31.00 (down from ₹47.89 in FY 2025). Revenue: ₹27.8b (up 14% from FY 2025). Net income: ₹3.26b (down 35% from FY 2025). Profit margin: 12% (down from 21% in FY 2025). The decrease in margin was driven by higher expenses. Revenue exceeded analyst estimates by 1.7%. Earnings per share (EPS) also surpassed analyst estimates by 7.5%. Revenue is forecast to grow 28% p.a. on average during the next 2 years, compared to a 2.9% growth forecast for the Banks industry in India.",
      "keyDevTypeId": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "raw_subtype": "BriefActivity"
    },
